## Open Questions

> 1. **Eligibility Scope**
>
>    * MVP recommendation: humanlike pawns only.
>    * Always include colonists.
>    * Include prisoners/slaves/guests if present on player maps.
>    * Hostile pawns can be included later or behind a setting to avoid save bloat.
> 2. **Snapshot Fidelity**
>
>    * MVP: identity, appearance, traits, skills, passions, backstories, ideology reference, basic health/body snapshot, and map/death context.
>    * Avoid equipment/inventory for MVP.
>    * Apparel/gear can be added later for higher-fidelity spirits if needed.
> 3. **Chronomancy Fresh Imprints**
>
>    * Should resurrection require a settled imprint at least 7 days old?
>    * Recommended: prefer an imprint at least 7 days old, but allow fresh imprints with harsher instability penalties if the spell tier permits it.
> 4. **Burial and Rites Compatibility**
>
>    * Aeternus rites should update the memory/death echo directly.
>    * Vanilla-style burial/sarcophagus containment should count as a compatibility-safe minimum rite, even if it is not the ideal Aeternus rite.

