## 7. Cleanup and Retention Policy

Cleanup should be conservative. Do not delete records merely because the pawn is despawned or absent from the current map.

### Keep Records If

* pawn is alive and tracked
* pawn is a colonist or important pawn
* pawn is in caravan or world-pawn state
* pawn is in cryptosleep or otherwise suspended
* corpse exists on map
* corpse is in grave/sarcophagus
* spirit is active
* record is bound, corrupted, or pending rites
* record is needed by Chronomancy or Aeternus systems

### Invalidate or Delete If

* corpse was cremated and lore says cremation releases/severs the imprint
* corpse was butchered/destroyed and no spiritual echo should remain
* non-colonist record has exceeded retention window
* hostile pawn left map alive and has no spirit/corpse/quest importance
* record is explicitly released and retention window has passed

Prefer marking records as `Released` or `Invalidated` before deletion so dependent systems can respond cleanly.

